{"version":"bonevision-github-pages-v1","source":"/Users/wangruoxuan/Downloads/Bone Break Classification","featureLength":125,"classes":[{"key":"avulsion","folder":"Avulsion fracture","zh":"撕脱性骨折","en":"Avulsion Fracture","ko":"견열 골절","desc_zh":"肌腱或韧带牵拉导致小骨片从主骨分离，常见于踝、指、髋周附着点。","desc_en":"A tendon or ligament pulls a small bone fragment away from the main bone, often near ankle, finger, or hip attachments.","desc_ko":"힘줄이나 인대의 견인으로 작은 골편이 주골에서 분리되는 골절로 발목, 손가락, 고관절 부착부에 흔합니다."},{"key":"comminuted","folder":"Comminuted fracture","zh":"粉碎性骨折","en":"Comminuted Fracture","ko":"분쇄 골절","desc_zh":"骨骼碎裂为三块或更多骨片，常由高能量创伤导致，影像上多条骨折线交叉。","desc_en":"The bone is broken into three or more fragments, usually after high-energy trauma with multiple intersecting fracture lines.","desc_ko":"고에너지 외상 후 뼈가 세 조각 이상으로 부서지며 여러 골절선이 교차하는 양상을 보입니다."},{"key":"fracture_dislocation","folder":"Fracture Dislocation","zh":"骨折脱位","en":"Fracture Dislocation","ko":"골절 탈구","desc_zh":"骨折伴随关节对位关系丧失，需关注神经血管受压和关节复位。","desc_en":"A fracture with loss of joint alignment; neurovascular compromise and joint reduction are key concerns.","desc_ko":"골절과 관절 정렬 소실이 동반되며 신경혈관 압박과 관절 정복 여부가 중요합니다."},{"key":"greenstick","folder":"Greenstick fracture","zh":"青枝骨折","en":"Greenstick Fracture","ko":"생나무 골절","desc_zh":"儿童常见，一侧骨皮质断裂而另一侧保持连续，表现为弯曲成角。","desc_en":"Common in children: one cortex breaks while the opposite cortex bends and remains continuous.","desc_ko":"소아에서 흔하며 한쪽 피질은 끊어지고 반대쪽 피질은 휘어진 채 유지됩니다."},{"key":"hairline","folder":"Hairline Fracture","zh":"发丝状骨折","en":"Hairline Fracture","ko":"모발선 골절","desc_zh":"细微裂隙或应力性骨折，骨皮质连续性仅轻度中断，X线表现可能很隐匿。","desc_en":"A very fine crack or stress fracture with subtle cortical interruption that may be faint on X-ray.","desc_ko":"매우 미세한 균열 또는 피로 골절로 X선에서 피질 중단이 희미하게 보일 수 있습니다."},{"key":"impacted","folder":"Impacted fracture","zh":"嵌顿性骨折","en":"Impacted Fracture","ko":"감입 골절","desc_zh":"骨折端相互嵌入，常伴局部骨密度增加或骨端短缩。","desc_en":"The broken bone ends are driven into each other, often with local density increase or shortening.","desc_ko":"골절된 양끝이 서로 밀려 들어가며 국소 골밀도 증가나 단축이 동반될 수 있습니다."},{"key":"longitudinal","folder":"Longitudinal fracture","zh":"纵向骨折","en":"Longitudinal Fracture","ko":"종방향 골절","desc_zh":"骨折线大致沿骨长轴走行，常需结合多视角判断延伸范围。","desc_en":"The fracture line runs roughly along the long axis of the bone and may require multi-view assessment.","desc_ko":"골절선이 뼈의 장축을 따라 주행하며 여러 촬영 방향으로 범위 확인이 필요할 수 있습니다."},{"key":"oblique","folder":"Oblique fracture","zh":"斜形骨折","en":"Oblique Fracture","ko":"사선 골절","desc_zh":"骨折线斜跨骨干，常由成角或剪切力导致，需评估移位程度。","desc_en":"A diagonal fracture line crosses the shaft, commonly from angulation or shear force; displacement matters.","desc_ko":"골절선이 골간을 비스듬히 가로지르며 각형성 또는 전단력에 의해 발생합니다."},{"key":"pathological","folder":"Pathological fracture","zh":"病理性骨折","en":"Pathological Fracture","ko":"병리적 골절","desc_zh":"基础骨病变导致骨强度下降后发生骨折，需评估肿瘤、骨质疏松或囊性病变。","desc_en":"A fracture through weakened bone from underlying disease such as tumor, osteoporosis, or cystic change.","desc_ko":"종양, 골다공증, 낭성 병변 등으로 약해진 뼈에서 발생하는 골절입니다."},{"key":"spiral","folder":"Spiral Fracture","zh":"螺旋形骨折","en":"Spiral Fracture","ko":"나선형 골절","desc_zh":"扭转力造成骨折线围绕骨干呈螺旋状走行，常见于长骨。","desc_en":"A twisting force creates a fracture line that spirals around the shaft, often in long bones.","desc_ko":"비틀림 힘으로 골절선이 골간을 나선형으로 감싸며 장골에서 흔합니다."}],"counts":{"avulsion":3,"comminuted":3,"fracture_dislocation":3,"greenstick":3,"hairline":3,"impacted":3,"longitudinal":3,"oblique":3,"pathological":3,"spiral":3},"prototypes":{"avulsion":[-0.21954,-0.07094,0.06402,0.13065,0.05784,-0.08736,-0.21507,-0.22312,-0.03434,0.12206,0.18194,0.11426,-0.05289,-0.21928,-0.20903,0.02327,0.17976,0.21649,0.13946,-0.0122,-0.20279,-0.19447,0.02625,0.17372,0.23281,0.14867,-0.0085,-0.20411,-0.17565,0.02019,0.15889,0.21855,0.15449,-0.01091,-0.19055,-0.14754,0.00207,0.10581,0.17339,0.13477,-0.01815,-0.15234,-0.14296,-0.02366,0.05199,0.09529,0.05775,-0.03389,-0.13508,0.00627,0.00641,0.00794,0.00874,0.00865,0.00796,0.00608,0